hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2267","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""When a person is performing prayer, he should not spit to his right or in front of him because he is supplicating before his Lord; rather, he should spit to his left or beneath his feet."
"2268","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw phlegm stuck (on the wall) in the direction of the Qiblah, so he took a pebble and scraped it off with it. Then he said: No one should ever spit in the direction of the Qiblah, nor to his right side. He should spit to his left side or under his left foot."
"2269","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a person stands to perform prayer, he should not spit in front of him because as long as he is engaged in prayer, he is supplicating before his Lord. He should also not spit to his right side because there is an angel on his right. He should spit to his left side or beneath his foot and bury it."
"2270","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to keep a stick in his hand. One day he entered the mosque. A stick was in his ha"
"2271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to keep a stick. He would hold it in his blessed hand. One day he entered the mosque, and"
"2272","'Abdullah b. Shakhkhir narrated it on the authority of his father that he said prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he spat and then rubbed it off with his left shoe. (Using translation from Muslim 554b)"
"2273","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When any one of you stands in prayer, let him not smooth the pebbles, for he is facing Mercy.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1191)"
"2274","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person stands to perform prayer, mercy faces him. Therefore, (while performing prayer) he should not move the pebbles (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) nor touch the pebbles."
"2275","""I asked Messenger of Allah (S) about smoothening the pebbles during Salat. He said: 'If you must do so, then let it be only once.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 380)"
"2276","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates: We used to perform prayer behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) during the intense heat of summer, so one of us would take pebbles in his palm. He would keep them in one hand, then in the other hand, and when they became cool, he would prostrate on them."""""
"2277","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Shibl Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: \""He forbade three things during prayer: pecking like a crow, spreading the feet like a beast, and that a person designates a specific place for sitting as a camel designates its sitting place.\"""""""
"2278","The Prophet said: ""A muslim does not regularly attend the mosques to perform prayer and remember Allah, but Allah feels happy with him just as the family of one who is absent feels happy when he comes back to them."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 800)"
"2279","Sa'id ibn AbuSa'id al-Maqburi reported on the authority of his father that he saw AbuRafi' the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, passing by Hasan ibn Ali (Allah be pleased with them) when he was standing offering his prayer. He had tied the back knot of his hair. AbuRafi' untied it. Hasan turned to him with anger, AbuRafi' said to him: Concentrate on your prayer and do not be angry: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: This is the seat of the devil, referring to the back knot of the hair. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 646)"
"2280","Kurayb the freed slave of Ibn Abbas reported: Abdullah ibn Abbas saw Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying having the back knot of the hair. He stood behind him and began to untie it. He remained standing unmoved (stationary). When he finished his prayer he came to Ibn Abbas and said to him: What were you doing with my head? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man who prays with the black knot of hair tied is the one praying pinioned. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 647)"
"2281","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Do not raise your gaze towards the sky during prayer, lest it be taken away.\"" The narrator says: That is, do not do this during prayer."""""
"2282","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does the person who raises his head before the Imam (from bowing or prostration)"
"2283","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Does the person who raises his head before the Imam (from bowing or prostration) not fear that Allah, the Exalted, will transform his head into the head of a dog?"
"2284","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What is the matter with people who lift their gaze to the sky when praying?"" And he spoke sternly concerning that until he said: ""They must stop that or they will certainly lose their eyesight."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1193)"
"2285","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man from performing prayer while placing his hand on his side (flank)."
"2286","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Placing the hand on the side during prayer is a way of seeking comfort used by the people of Hell."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: What is meant by this is that this is the practice of the Jews and Christians, and those people are the people of Hell.)"
"2287","I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about looking to the sides during prayer. He said: It is something which the devil snatches from a servant’s prayers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 910)"
"2288","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to glance to the right and to the left during prayer, but he would not turn his neck to look beh"
"2289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade letting the garment hang down (sadl) during prayer."
"2290","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade al-Ishtimal as-Sammaa."
"2291","I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment crossing the two ends. (Using translation from Muslim 518a)"
"2292","It was narrated from Umar bin Abi Salamah that he saw Messenger of Allah ﷺpraying in a single garment in the house of Umm Salamah, putting the ends of it on his shoulders."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 764)"
"2293","narrates: He came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing prayer in a single garment, the edges of which he had thrown over his shoulders in opposite directions."
"2294",""" I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I go hunting wearing nothing but a single shirt. Can I pray in it?' He said: 'Fasten it to yourself even with a thorn.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 765)"
"2295","Does every one of you has two garment? (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 625)"
"2296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do all of you have two garments?"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the person who had asked him this question, ""Do you know Abu Hurairah? Sometimes he performs prayer in a single garment while his other clothes are hanging on the peg."
"2297","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: Does each one of you have two (garments)?"
"2298","I think he also mentioned pajamas."
"2299","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs prayer in a single garment should wrap it around himself."
"2300","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also led prayer in this manner."
"2301","The men used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ with their Izars tied around their necks as boys used to do; therefore the Prophet ﷺ told the women not to raise their heads till the men sat down straight (while praying). (Using translation from Bukhārī 362)"
"2302","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing prayer in a single garment, which he had wrapped around himself as an ishtimal (envelopment)."
"2303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He should wrap it around himself like a sheikh and then perform prayer in it."
"2304","if anyone prays in a single piece of cloth, he should cross the two ends. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 627)"
"2305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you are about to perform prayer and you have only one garment on your body, if it is wide, then wear it as an al-ihtifaf (enveloping oneself), and if it is narrow, then tie it as an izar (lower garment)."
"2306","I think these words are also in the narration: (perform prayer) in pajamas."
"2307","narrates: He came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing prayer on a mat. He was prostrating on it."
"2308","""I heard Anas Bin Malik say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mix with us so much that he said to a little brother of mine: ""O Abu ʿUmair, what happened to the Nughair (one of the narrators Wakiʿ said that it means a bird that he used to play with)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3720)"
"2309","Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a household among the Ansars, and he took a meal with them. When he intended to leave, he asked for a place in that house for him, to pray so a mat sprinkled with water was put and he offered prayer over it, and invoked for Allah's Blessing upon them (his hosts). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6080)"
"2310","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform prayer on a mat."
"2311","It was narrated from Maimunah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a mat. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 738)"
"2312","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform prayer on a mat."
"2313","""I have been honored over the Prophets with six (things): I have been given Jawami' Al-Kalam, I have been aided by (the ability to cause in the enemy) fright, the spoils of war have been made lawful for me, the Earth has been made as a Masjid and purifier for me, and I have been sent to all creatures, and with me Prophethood is sealed."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1553)"
"2314","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If you cannot find anywhere (for prayer) except sheep's resting-places and camels' resting-places, then perform prayer in the sheep's resting-places and do not perform prayer in the camels' resting-places."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 768)"
"2315","It was narrated from Abu Sa’eed that the Prophet ﷺ forbade building structures over graves. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1564)"
"2316","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'All the earth is a mosque, except for graveyards and Hammam.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 745)"
"2317","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If you cannot find anywhere (for prayer) except sheep's resting-places and camels' resting-places, then perform prayer in the sheep's resting-places and do not perform prayer in the camels' resting-places."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 768)"
"2318","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering over graves.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1562)"
"2319","""I heard Ibn 'Umar say: 'We used to sell grain before it was ripe and before it was evident that it was free of disease and blight (by means of Al-Mukhabarah). We did not see anything wrong with that, until Rafi' bin Khadij said that the Messenger of Allah had forbidden Al-Mukhabarah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3917)"
"2320","Do not sit on the graves and do not pray facing towards them. (Using translation from Muslim 972a)"
"2321","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'All the earth is a mosque, except for graveyards and Hammam.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 745)"
"2322","It was narrated from Abu Sa’eed that the Prophet ﷺ forbade building structures over graves. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1564)"
"2323","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade offering prayer facing towards graves."
"2324","Do not pray facing towards the graves, and do not sit on them. (Using translation from Muslim 972b)"
"2325","The worst of people are those whom the Hour will overtake (i.e., upon whom the Hour will be established), and those who take graves as mosques."
"2326","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah's curse to be on the Jews, they made the graves of their Prophets mosques. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3227)"
"2327","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah's curse to be on the Jews, they made the graves of their Prophets mosques. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3227)"
"2328","Messenger of Allah ﷺ came over to Medina and encamped at the upper side of Medina among the tribe known as Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. He stayed among them for fourteen days. He then sent someone to call Banu al-Najjar. They came to him hanging their swords from the necks. Anas then said: As if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting on his mount and Abu Bakr seated behind him, and Banu al-Najjar standing around him. He descended in the courtyard of Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say his prayer in the folds of the sheep and goats. He commanded us to build a mosque. He then sent for Banu al-Najjar and said to them: Banu al-Najjar, sell this land of yours to me for some price. They replied: By Allah, we do not want any price (from you) except from Allah. Anas said: I tell what this land contained. It contained the graves of the disbelievers, dung-hills, and some trees of date-palm. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded and the graves of the disbelievers were dug open, and the trees of the date-palm were cut off. The wood of the date-palm were erected in front of the mosque ; the door-steps wre built of stone. They were reciting verses carrying the stones. The Prophet ﷺ also joined them (in reciting verses) saying: O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter. So grant you aid to the Ansar and the Muhajirah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 453)"
"2329","I think the words in the narration are, ""and that woman would be in a state of menstruation at that time."
"2330","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to offer prayer in our blanket."
"2331","Mu'awiyah ibn AbuSufyan asked his sister Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: Would the apostle of Allah ﷺ pray in the clothe in which he had an intercourse? She said: Yes, when he would not see any impurity in it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 366)"
"2332","Aswad bin Yazid narrates: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) saw me washing the traces of janabah from my garment. She asked: What is this? I replied: This is the trace of janabah that got on my garment. So Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I remember this about myself, it would also get on the garment of the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he would say, we would scrape it off like this."
"2333","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), \""Can I perform prayer in the garment in which I had intercourse with my wife?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes, but if you see anything on it, then wash it.\"""""""
"2334","It was narrated from Awn bin Abi Juhaifah, from his father that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in a red Hullah, and he set up a short spear (Anazah) and prayed facing toward it, while dogs, women and donkeys were passing beyond it. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 772)"
"2335","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came, and he was leaning on Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he was wearing a Qatari cloak, which he had wrapped as an adornment. He led the people in prayer."
"2336","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did not perform prayer in our small or large sheets."
"2337","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to perform prayer, and he was wearing a cloak which had patterns on it. The sight of those patterns is as if still before my eyes today. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) completed the prayer, he said: Take this cloak to Abu Juham bin Hudhaifah and bring me his plain cloak, because this cloak tried to distract me in my prayer."
"2338","I feared that my attention would become distracted."
"2339","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying Sayyidah Umamah (may Allah be pleased with her) during the prayer. When he would go into ruku (bowing), he would put her down to stand, then he would go into sajdah (prostration). When he stood up again, he would pick her up again, and when he was about to go into ruku, he would put her down to stand again."
"2340","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came for prayer while he was carrying Sayyidah Umamah bint Abi Al-As (may Allah be pleased with her) on his shoulder. When he went into bowing (ruku‘), he put her down from his shoulder, and when he finished his prostration (sajdah), he picked her up again onto his shoulder. He continued doing this until he finished the prayer."
"2341","I would be lying on the bedding between him and the Qiblah, in the widthwise direction. This was the bedding upon which the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his wife used to rest."
"2342","""I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and my feet were in the direction of his Qiblah. When he prostrated he nudged me and I drew up my feet, then when he stood up I stretched them out again. And there were no lamps in the houses at the time."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 168)"
"2343","I used to sleep with my legs in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he would offer his prayer at night (i.e. tahajjud prayer offered towards the end of the night.). When he prostrated himself he struck my legs, and I drew them up and he then prostrated. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 712)"
"2344",""" "" . Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform prayer at night, and I would be lying between him and the Qiblah. When he intended to perform Witr, he would wake me up."
"2346","I would be lying in front of him, in the direction of the Qiblah, across its width. When he intended to perform Witr, he would move me by touching me with his foot."
"2347","I would be lying between him and the Qiblah. When he intended to perform Witr, he would wake me up, and then I would also perform Witr."
"2348","I used to stretch my feet in the direction of the Qiblah in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He would be performing prayer at that time. When he intended to go into prostration, he would nudge me, so I would draw in my feet. Then when he stood up, I would stretch them out again."",""Note: The phrase """"peace be upon him"""" is for the honorific term """"صلى الله عليه وسلم"""" (sallallahu aleihi wasallam)"",""commonly abbreviated as ﷺ in English."""""
"2349","I caught him by the throat and strangled him until I felt the coolness of his tongue on my palm. If it were not for my brother Solomon’s (peace be upon him) supplication, he (the devil) would have been tied up until morning and you people would have seen him."
"2350","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw Satan during prayer, he caught him and strangled him, until he felt the coolness of his tongue on his blessed hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If it were not for the supplication of my brother, Sayyiduna Sulaiman (peace be upon him), he (Satan) would have been tied up so that people could see him."
"2351","The Prophet ﷺ said: Kill the two black things during prayer, the snake and scorpion. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 921)"
"2352","The Prophet ﷺ said: Kill the two black things during prayer, the snake and scorpion. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 921)"
"2353","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade letting a garment hang loosely as a covering (sadal) during prayer and for a man to cover his face."
"2354","we used to pray along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in intense heat. When any of us could not rest his face on bare ground while prostrating due to intense heat he spread his cloth and would prostrate on it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 660)"
"2355","""I knocked at the door when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was offering a voluntary prayer. The door was in the direction of the Qiblah so he took a few steps to his right or left and opened the door, then he went back to where he was praying."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1206)"
"2356","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was leading the people in prayer when two girls from the descendants of Abdul Muttalib came running; they were quarreling with each other. The Prophet (peace be upon him) caught hold of them and separated one from the other. He did not mind this at all."
"2357","The yawning as from the devil. So when one of you yawns he should try to restrain it as far as it lies in his power. (Using translation from Muslim 2994)"
"2358","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty likes sneezing and dislikes yawning. So when any one of you feels like yawning, he should try his best to restrain it, or else place his hand over his mouth, because when he yawns and says 'Ah', Satan laughs within him (as a result of which this sound comes out)."
"2359","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Yawning during prayer is from Satan; when a person feels this situation, he should try to restrain it."
"2360","When one of you yawns, he should hold his hand over his mouth, for the devil enters. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5026)"
"2361","“When anyone of you performs prayer, let him put something in front of him. If he cannot find anything then let him put a stick. If he cannot find one, then let him draw a line. Then it will not matter if anything passes in front of him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 943)"
"2362","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should only perform prayer facing a sutrah, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If they do not comply, then fight with them, for he will be a devil."
"2363","""I saw the Prophet when he had completed his seven (circuits of Tawaf); he came to the edge of the Mataf and prayed two Rakahs, with nothing in between him and people who were circumambulating."" (Daif) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2959)"
"2364","The narrator named Kathir bin Kathir is Kathir bin Kathir bin Mutlib bin Abu Wada'ah bin Sabirah bin Sa'id bin Sa'd bin Sahm bin Amr bin Hasees bin Ka'b bin Lu'ayy Sahmi."
"2365","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a person were to know how much sin there is in passing in front of his brother while he is supplicating to his Lord (i.e., performing prayer), then it would be more beloved to him to stand in that place for one hundred years than to take a single step (and pass in front of his brother)."
"2366","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: ""If one who passes in front of a man who is praying knew the responsibility he incurs, he would prefer to stand still for forty. . . rather than pass in front of him. Abu al-Nadr said: I do not know whether he said forty days, or months, or years."" Abu Dawud: Sufyan al-Thawri said: If a man passes proudly in front of me while I am praying, I shall stop him, and if a weak man passes, I shall not stop him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 701)"
"2367","When one of you prays, he should not let anyone pass in front of him; he should turn him away as far as possible; but if he refuses (to go), he should fight him, for he is only a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 697)"
"2368","When one of you prays, he should not let anyone pass in front of him; he should turn him away as far as possible; but if he refuses (to go), he should fight him, for he is only a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 697)"
"2369","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You people should only perform prayer facing a sutrah, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he does not comply, then a person should quarrel with him, for with that (other) person will be a devil."
"2370","When any one of you prays, he should not allow anyone to pass before him, and if he refuses, he should be then forcibly resisted, for there is a devil with him. (Using translation from Muslim 506a)"
"2371","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was performing prayer. A goat passed in front of him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) compelled it to go towards the Qiblah (the wall in the direction of prayer), until he made its belly touch the Qiblah (the wall in the direction of prayer)."
"2372","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When anyone of you performs prayer, let him pray facing towards a Sutrah, and let him get close to it, and not let anyone pass in front of him. If someone comes and wants to pass in front of him, let him fight him, for he is a Shaitan (satan).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 954)"
"2373","""When anyone of you prays toward a Sutra, let him get close to it and not allow the Shaitan to sever his prayer for him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 748)"
"2374","The distance between the Musalla of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the wall was just sufficient for a sheep to pass through . (Using translation from Bukhārī 496)"
"2375","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When anyone of you performs prayer, let him pray facing towards a Sutrah, and let him get close to it, and not let anyone pass in front of him. If someone comes and wants to pass in front of him, let him fight him, for he is a Shaitan (satan).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 954)"
"2376","The Prophet ﷺ said: When one of you prays, he should put something in front of his face, and if he can find nothing , he should set up his staff; but if he has no staff, he should draw a line; then what passes in front of him will not harm him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 689)"
"2377","narrates: A spear was fixed for the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he performed prayer facing towards it."
"2378","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) facing his mount and performing prayer. Nafi’ narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) facing his mount and performing prayer."
"2379","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When one of you places in front of him so me. thing such as the back of a saddle, he should pray without caring who passes on the other side of it. (Using translation from Muslim 499a)"
"2380","“We used to perform prayer while the beasts were passing in front of us. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: ‘If something like the hand of a saddle* is placed in front of anyone of you, it will not matter whoever passes in front of him.” * It is the piece of wood on the camel saddle which is held on to (to climb onto the camel). (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 940)"
"2381","I and a young man from Banu Abdul Muttalib came riding a donkey, one in front and one behind. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was leading the people in prayer in an open field at that time. We left the donkey in front of the people, then we came and joined the row. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not mind this at all."
